# EKS Infrastructure – Allegro Project

## ⚠️ NOTE: S3 Backend Configuration
This project uses a remote state stored in S3 with a lock in DynamoDB.

### Infrastructure parameters:
- **Region:** `eu-north-1`
- **Bucket Name:** `allegro-analytics-eks-tfstate-2026`
- **DynamoDB Table:** `terraform-state-lock`
- **Secrets Manager** `allegro-app-secrets-dev` for development and `allegro-app-secrets-prod` for production

### Synchronization instructions:
The same bucket name **MUST** appear in two places:
1. `.bootstrap/variables.tf` -> variable `state_bucket_name`
2. `./backend.tf` -> the `bucket` parameter in the `backend “s3”` block

---

## Setup steps:
### 1. Go to `.bootstrap/` and run `terraform apply`.
### 2. Go to  `envs/dev/` and run `terraform apply`.
### 3. Go to AWS and SSM into mgmt-asg EC2 and configure it:
 
```
#Update kubeconfig
aws eks update-kubeconfig --name allegro-analytics-eks-dev-eks-cluster --region eu-north-1

# Cilium
CILIUM_CLI_VERSION=$(curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cilium/cilium-cli/main/stable.txt)
CLI_ARCH=amd64
if [ "$(uname -m)" = "aarch64" ]; then CLI_ARCH=arm64; fi
curl -L --fail --remote-name-all https://github.com/cilium/cilium-cli/releases/download/${CILIUM_CLI_VERSION}/cilium-linux-${CLI_ARCH}.tar.gz{,.sha256sum}
sha256sum --check cilium-linux-${CLI_ARCH}.tar.gz.sha256sum
sudo tar xzvfC cilium-linux-${CLI_ARCH}.tar.gz /usr/local/bin
rm cilium-linux-${CLI_ARCH}.tar.gz{,.sha256sum}

### 4. Install Cilium
kubectl cluster-info
<!-- remove the “https://”  -->
helm repo add cilium https://helm.cilium.io/
helm install cilium cilium/cilium --version 1.17.4 \
  --namespace kube-system \
  --set eni.enabled=true \
  --set ipam.mode=eni \
  --set egressMasqueradeInterfaces="ens+" \
  --set routingMode=native\
  --set kubeProxyReplacement=true\
  --set k8sServiceHost=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.gr7.eu-north-1.eks.amazonaws.com\
  --set k8sServicePort=443

### 5. After running Cilium - Delete AWS VPC CNI
kubectl delete ds aws-node -n kube-system
kubectl delete ds kube-proxy -n kube-system

#### Comment "cluster_addons" in "module/eks/variables.tf"
    # vpc-cni = {
    #   most_recent = true
    #   before_compute = true 
    # }
    # kube-proxy = {
    #   most_recent = true
    #   before_compute = true
    # }

helm repo add argoproj https://argoproj.github.io/argo-helm
helm repo update

helm upgrade --install argocd argoproj/argo-cd \
  --namespace argocd \
  --create-namespace \
  --set configs.params.server\.insecure=true

sudo git clone -b testing https://github.com/Rehox0/allegro-analytics-eks.git
kubectl apply -f ~/allegro-analytics-eks/k8s/root-app.yaml

```
---

##ArgoCD UI
Locally run:
aws ssm start-session \
  --target i-xxxxxxxxxxxxx \
  --document-name AWS-StartPortForwardingSession \
  --parameters '{"portNumber":["8080"],"localPortNumber":["8080"]}'

On mgmt:
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443




### Run workflow
Use `Terraform OIDC + SSM` workflow (`workflow_dispatch`) and choose:
- `environment`: `dev|prod`
- `operation`: `plan|apply|destroy` (`destroy` allowed only for `dev`)
- `aws_region`: AWS region for OIDC + SSM calls (default `eu-north-1`)
- `ref`: branch/tag/SHA

The workflow assumes role via OIDC, finds `mgmt-asg` instance, then runs Terraform remotely over SSM in:
- `Terraform_EKS/envs/<environment>`

## GitHub Actions + OIDC (Bootstrap-managed)

Required variables in `.bootstrap`:

```hcl
github_owner      = "OWNER_OR_ORG"
github_repository = "REPO_NAME"
github_token      = "ghp_xxx..." # token with rights to manage environment secrets
```


## Private-only cluster defaults
- EKS API endpoint is private-only (`endpoint_public_access = false`).
- ALB exposure is internal-only by convention and restricted to internal CIDR ranges passed in `alb_ingress_cidr_blocks`.
- Terraform apply for environments should run from the management EC2 in VPC (or through SSM).


The Draft:

rsync -avzL --delete --progress --exclude '.terraform' --exclude '.git' --exclude '.bootstrap' --exclude '*.tfstate*' ./allegro-analytics-eks/ ec2-user@i-0b9f96ab0ba0d5335:/home/ec2-user/allegro-analytics-eks/


WARNING!!
Local device are UNABLE to see the resources in EKS cluster. Therefore, there may be a drift in the `terraform plan`
